ROW_NUMBER does not have any argument. It will simply assign an integer row number as per the ORDER BY clause.

Requirement: Top 3 Materials by Sales Value per Customer using HANA Ranking
Data:
Customer Material SalesValue
--------------------------------
1000     MAT1     250000
1000     MAT2     180000
1000     MAT3     120000
1000     MAT4      90000
2000     MAT8     400000
2000     MAT1     320000
2000     MAT6     150000

Solution:

SELECT *
FROM
(
    SELECT

        vbrk.kunag AS Customer,
        vbrp.matnr AS Material,
        SUM(vbrp.netwr) AS SalesValue,

        ROW_NUMBER()
          OVER
          (
             PARTITION BY vbrk.kunag    // creates independent ranking for every customer
             ORDER BY SUM(vbrp.netwr) DESC
          ) AS RankNo

    FROM vbrk

    INNER JOIN vbrp
      ON vbrk.vbeln = vbrp.vbeln

    GROUP BY
       vbrk.kunag,
       vbrp.matnr

) X

WHERE RankNo <= 3;

Result:
Customer Material Sales Rank
--------------------------------
1000     MAT1     250000   1
1000     MAT2     180000   2
1000     MAT3     120000   3

2000     MAT8     400000   1
2000     MAT1     320000   2
2000     MAT6     150000   3

2. Usage of ROW_NUMBER( )

SELECT FROM /dmo/flight
       FIELDS
           carrier_id,
           connection_id,
           seats_occupied,
           ROW_NUMBER( ) OVER( PARTITION BY carrier_id
                               ORDER BY seats_occupied ) AS so_row,
           ROW_NUMBER( ) OVER( PARTITION BY carrier_id
                               ORDER BY flight_date ) AS fldate_row
       INTO TABLE @DATA(lt_window).



- can use this ROW_NUMBER( ) multiple times to get row number with different sort order but the result set will be sorted by per the sort order used for last partition.
